# EMI Payment — Implementation Plan

## Overview

Implement a full EMI (Equated Monthly Installments) system for high-value orders. Buyers split a large order into N monthly payments. Admins configure EMI plans. Stripe and Razorpay collect each installment.

---

## Architecture

```
Admin configures EMI Plans (e.g. "3-Month 0%", "6-Month 2%", "12-Month 5%")
       ↓
Buyer at Checkout sees EMI options when cart ≥ min_order_amount
       ↓
Buyer selects a plan → first installment charged immediately via Stripe/Razorpay
       ↓
EmiSchedule created with remaining installments as "scheduled"
       ↓
Buyer pays remaining installments from their dashboard
       ↓
Order fulfilment begins after first installment is paid
```

---

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **First installment at checkout**: The first installment is charged immediately. Remaining installments are due monthly and paid manually from the dashboard. Is this correct, or should it be fully automatic recurring billing?

> [!NOTE]
> **Overdue handling**: Overdue installments are flagged but the order is not blocked. No penalty — can be extended later.

